<Base title="Privacy — NetRelish" description="What this site does with your email, and what it doesn’t do.">
  <main class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>This site sets no cookies, and your browser loads nothing from a third-party domain. It does count visits: Vercel Web Analytics, whose script is served from netrelish.com itself, records which page you landed on and which site you came from. It sets no cookie. It tells visits apart by a hash of each request, which Vercel discards after a day, so it cannot recognize you from one day to the next or follow you anywhere else. Vercel hosts this site and holds those counts for us.</p>
    <p>If you join the beta list, your email goes to Bento, the mailing tool we use, tagged for the NetRelish beta. It is used for beta invites and launch news, nothing else, and is never sold or shared. If you buy Pro here for the direct-download build, Stripe handles the payment: your email, billing details and card go to Stripe, and your card number never reaches us. Your license key is then kept with your email in Bento so it can be emailed to you. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and you can ask for your address to be deleted at any time by replying to one.</p>
    <p>The app is a different matter, and a simpler one: NetRelish makes no network calls except the pages you load, the App Store, a one-time license activation if you bought the direct-download build, and — on Pro — a signed timestamp for your sealed pages. Your browsing data never leaves your Mac.</p>
    <p><a href="/">Back to NetRelish</a></p>
  </div></main>
</Base>
